A certain linear, time-invariant system has the state and output representation shown below:
$$$\eqalign{
  &amp; \left[ {\matrix{
   {\mathop {{x_1}}\limits^ \bullet  }  \cr 
   {\mathop {{x_2}}\limits^ \bullet  }  \cr 

 } } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
   { - 2} &amp; 1  \cr 
   0 &amp; { - 3}  \cr 

 } } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
   {{x_1}}  \cr 
   {{x_2}}  \cr 

 } } \right] + \left[ {\matrix{
   1  \cr 
   0  \cr 

 } } \right]u  \cr 
  &amp; y = \left( {\matrix{
   1 &amp; 1  \cr 

 } } \right)\left[ {\matrix{
   {{x_1}}  \cr 
   {{x_2}}  \cr 

 } } \right] \cr} $$$
<br>(a) Find the eigen values (natural frequencies) of the system.
<br>(b)If u(t)=$$\delta \left( t \right)$$ and x<sub>1</sub>(0<sup>+</sup>)=x<sub>2</sub>(0<sup>+</sup>)=0, find x<sub>1</sub>(t),x<sub>2</sub>(t) and y(t), for t&gt;0.
<br>(c)When the input is zero, choose initial conditions $${x_1}\left( {{0^ + }} \right)$$ and $${x_2}\left( {{0^ + }} \right)$$ such that $$y\left( t \right) = A{e^{ - 2t}}$$ for t&gt;0

The eigen values of the matrix $$\left[ {\matrix{
   2 &amp; { - 1} &amp; 0 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 3 &amp; 0 &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 0 &amp; { - 2} &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 0 &amp; { - 1} &amp; 4  \cr 

 } } \right]$$ are

$$\int\limits_0^{{\raise0.5ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle \pi $}
\kern-0.1em/\kern-0.15em
\lower0.25ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle 2$}}} {\int\limits_0^{{\raise0.5ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle \pi $}
\kern-0.1em/\kern-0.15em
\lower0.25ex\hbox{$\scriptstyle 2$}}} {\sin \left( {x + y} \right)dx\,dy} } $$

en.explanation:
Current flowing through inductor,
<br/><br/>$$
I(t)=e^{a t}+e^{b t}
$$
<br/><br/>Voltage across inductor,
<br/><br/>$$
\begin{aligned}
&V(t)=L \frac{d I(t)}{d t}=1 \frac{d}{d t}\left[e^{a t}+e^{b t}\right] \\\\
&V(t)=a e^{a t}+b e^{b t}
\end{aligned}
$$

Since diode is Forward Bias, so it will be replaced by short circuit wire, and now applying KCL for voltage V.<br/><br/> $\frac{V-4}{2}+\frac{V}{2}+\frac{V+2}{2}=0$
<br/><br/>$$
\begin{aligned}
 \Rightarrow &V=\frac{2}{3} \\\\
&V_0=-V=\frac{-2}{3}
\end{aligned}
$$
